From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:20:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] updater: delete its key when it uninstalls for lack of apps

Uninstalling with --uninstall-if-unused deleted ClientState but left the
updater's own Clients entries and install values, including an
UninstallCmdLine naming the deleted updater.exe. Once no app remains, the
whole key goes. Found by Ghost's end-to-end test.

Why: upstream leaves the updater's own registration behind.
Upstream: not yet filed; a candidate for upstreaming
Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/chrome/updater/win/setup/uninstall.cc b/chrome/updater/win/setup/uninstall.cc
index 891b050b9eae6ef9f1c9bd75beb23238d451fb68..0ebccca2e2c929919014e46b75c707810fea8889 100644
--- a/chrome/updater/win/setup/uninstall.cc
+++ b/chrome/updater/win/setup/uninstall.cc
@@ -121,8 +121,27 @@ void DeleteClientStateKey(UpdaterScope scope) {
   }
 }
 
+// Ghost: once no app remains (`--uninstall-if-unused`), the updater's whole
+// key goes, with its own `Clients` entries and its install values, so that
+// uninstalling leaves no registration behind.
+void DeleteUpdaterKeyIfUnused(UpdaterScope scope) {
+  if (!base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch(
+          kUninstallIfUnusedSwitch)) {
+    return;
+  }
+  const HKEY root = UpdaterScopeToHKeyRoot(scope);
+  for (const auto& access_mask : {KEY_WOW64_32KEY, KEY_WOW64_64KEY}) {
+    base::win::RegKey company;
+    if (company.Open(root, COMPANY_KEY, KEY_QUERY_VALUE | access_mask) ==
+        ERROR_SUCCESS) {
+      company.DeleteKey(L"Update");
+    }
+  }
+}
+
 void DeleteGoogleUpdateFilesAndKeys(UpdaterScope scope) {
   DeleteClientStateKey(scope);
+  DeleteUpdaterKeyIfUnused(scope);
 
   const std::optional<base::FilePath> target_path =
       GetGoogleUpdateExePath(scope);
